  "notes": [
    "Chaos run: More closed-loop clients than the cluster has request slots for the length of the fault window: the workers' slots and queues fill and the gateway answers 503.",
    "What this embedded mock cluster cannot show here: What a real queue in the gateway does (Phase 15 D11): on master there is none, so this shows the rejections the clients get. Closed-loop clients also back off on a 503, which softens the overload an open-loop crowd would cause.",
    "Windows follow when the fault was really applied and cleared. Gateway counters (attempts per request, retries) are read at the tick that opens and closes a window (every 1s), so an attempt of a request in flight at a boundary falls in the next window; the per-request figures come from the clients.",
    "Closed-loop clients: 19 for the whole run, plus 29 in the fault window on 32 request slots (32 left serving). Closed-loop clients wait for each response, so a failing worker also slows the offered load.",
    "Load average (1, 5 and 15 minutes) at the start of the run: 4.74 4.66 4.51; at the end: 4.25 4.55 4.47."
  ],
